ries reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other\". Good, with quote on page 4.\n\nSearch methods: \"initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach\" → search_methods: [\"google_scholar\",\"snowballing\"]. Page 5.\n\nI can write the overview note now with evidence from page 4 and page 5. Let me write that note, then continue recalling pending.\n\nActually I should be careful about budget: one action per turn. Let me write the overview note now (ev-26c9... for categories on page 4, ev-dbca... for search methods page 5).\n\nBut wait — writing a note might be better after more reading to consolidate. However writing overview now is fine since I have both answers with exact quotes.\n\nLet me do that, and combine with recall? Better to keep it a single action: write_note. But the instruction says one fenced block; I can do both write_note and recall in one block. Yes, they're independent-ish. Let me do write_note then recall pending.\n\nActually recall will deliver evidence in the next turn; fine.\n\nLet me craft the note content (80-1500 chars) including answers, page numbers, exact quotes.\n\nNote content (English quotes):\n\n\"overview: Categories = reasoning, acting, interacting (p.4: 'The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other'). Literature search (p.5): 'The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.' So search_methods = google_scholar, snowballing. Note survey excludes multi-agent work without LLMs.\"\n\nGood, under 1500.\n\nAlso I need the exact quote for categories to include all three categories; the sentence \"The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other\" supports all three. Good, but ensure ≥20 chars, yes.\n\nNow recall pending ids. Let's do it."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {