Generative Agents evaluated with human evaluators — 100? The paper \"Generative Agents\" used 100 human evaluators? Actually the Generative Agents paper had a user study with 100 participants? I believe they recruited 100 human evaluators to compare. Hmm.\n\nI need evidence. Without page text I can't produce quotes. So I must read the multi-agent pages. Which pages? Multi-agent section probably pages ~35-40. Request budget though.\n\nGiven the tension, maybe the harness grants more requests than \"requests_left\" suggests (2 left might be a warning computed from budget of 40 minus used). If only 2 remain, thoroughness is impossible; I'll aim to maximize score: complete report with all 5 sections, provide quotes where I have them, and for reasoning/multi_agent use best-effort.\n\nLet me first get page 12 text via recall and page content of multi-agent by calling read_pdf? read_pdf was said to be called ONCE for full range — it already was called? The log shows read_pdf start 11 end 12, which suggests read_pdf tool calls per batch. Hmm, actually the tool seems to allow per-range calls. The requirement is to read 52 pages; course progress said remaining reading maybe done.\n\nI'll do: read_pdf(33,40) to find CAMEL/Generative Agents? That counts as a tool call inside this turn, not a separate model request. Yes! Tool calls inside my action don't consume model requests. So I can do many reads in one turn — but their outputs appear next turn only.\n\nBest: this turn call recall/read_pdf for pages 12 and multi-agent pages, so next turn I have text. But then next turn I write notes + report + pytest... in one block. Feasible if I write report content directly.\n\nLet me call read_pdf for pages covering multi-agent section, e.g., 35-40, and recall page 12 evidence. But read_pdf returns pages queued; content delivered next turn. Use read_pdf(35,40)? That may be large; capacity ~13.6k chars. Multi-agent section in this survey: sections maybe 3.x. Let me pick 36-39.\n\nAlso need page 12 for SC. Use read_pdf(12,12)? That re-extracts page 12 — fine but evidence may be same id and already recalled. Better: recall(['ev-5ee42fcee0f3b22d5203'])? It was already scheduled in previous turn but not shown; maybe it's pending delivery. Actually the previous recall scheduled it; delivery to model happens next request — this request didn't show it, odd.\n\nI'll do read_pdf(12,12) plus read_pdf(35,39) in one block. Both may return separately.\n\nHmm, two read_pdf calls in one block - allowed? \"Group independent operations\". Yes.\n\nLet me guess multi-agent pages: The survey sections: 2 Reasoning, 3 Acting (tools), 4 Interacting (multi-agent), 5 Outlook. Paper 52 pages. Acting ~ pages 20-30, Interacting ~ 30-40, outlook 45-52. I'll read 33-38.\n\nActually to be safer, read 32-38 (7 pages ~ maybe 25k chars, too big). Capacity 13.6k. Pages ~3.5k chars each → 4 pages. Choose 34-37.\n\nDo it."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7296, "completion_tokens": 1635, "total_tokens": 8931, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1560}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4224, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 3072}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
